  "prompt_text": "The figure is a conceptual overview linking location-specific conditions of bioenergy or crop production to the kinds of impacts that should be assessed. In the center, a stylized agricultural landscape shows crops, roots, soil, groundwater, a farmhouse, power lines, and a conversion plant, suggesting a full land-to-processing system.\n\nOn the left, the figure lists parameters that vary by place and management: climate conditions, distance to the conversion plant, historical land use, crop management, soil characteristics, and water availability. These are presented as inputs or contextual factors that shape system performance.\n\nOn the right, the figure shows the resulting impact categories, spanning environmental, economic, and social dimensions. Visible examples include greenhouse gas emissions, economic performance or costs, rural development, food security, biodiversity, and effects on soil and water. The arrangement implies that local site conditions influence multiple outcomes simultaneously, rather than a single metric.\n\nThe legend distinguishes examples suggested by a previous study from additional examples, indicating that the framework expands earlier recommendations. Overall, the figure emphasizes that evaluating such land-based production systems requires a site-specific, multi-criteria perspective that connects local parameters to a broad set of sustainability impacts.",
